    "summary": "docs/daemon.md gains a section on what a plan-tree run does about scope, failed tasks and runs that died; its note for clients says the separate IDE repository is no longer maintained (the stakeholder's instruction of 2026-10-08) and names the two plugins in this repository. Live runs, all on 2026-10-09 through the installed daemon at 6dc1ccca, one at a time: infra S completed (7 tasks, 0 failed); data S completed with a report (4 of 6 tasks failed, the report written from what existed); code S completed with a report whose first line names the eight failed functional-surface tasks t04 to t11; infra S with an empty prompt completed (unfocused intent); infra M (twice) and infra L completed with no planner-kind task, so the nested integration test in walker-aggregate.test.ts is the proof of ac2; docs S failed at the aggregate task with executor-aggregator-failed (input over 10MB for one model call), the exception accepted on 2026-10-08, to be closed by Story s3. The four suites compared by name with the baseline: no test that passed then fails now; eight tests of the removed scope functions are gone, and one daemon test was retitled by task t14. Mishaps: a first client without the stream flag ran nothing; the first infra run was killed with its session and recorded as aborted; size M ran twice because an unseen earlier turn of the session was still alive.",
